From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:14:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] accel/tcg: forget the plugin callback's return address and
 flags after a longjmp

A callback that leaves through cpu_loop_exit (qemu_plugin_set_pc, a raised
guest fault) left cpu->neg.plugin_cb_ra, tcg_hook_ra and the callback's
register flags set.  A later faulting plugin read, or a set_pc from a context
that sets none of them (a syscall event, the KVM path), then unwound against
the earlier, unrelated block: a wrong PC or cc_op, or the fault raised at the
wrong instruction.  Clear them in cpu_exec_longjmp_cleanup.  (The syscall
event entry, src/plugins/syscall-system.c, now zeroes ra itself.)

Review blocker 1 (review-notes/qemu_builder-panda-next.md).
---
 accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c b/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
index 257211235dbb94d6d9cce1862126bc248c399f17..b777f094c957abaaa712ac6649c2ee641724fb5a 100644
--- a/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
@@ -542,6 +542,18 @@ static void cpu_exec_longjmp_cleanup(CPUState *cpu)
         tb_unlock_pages(tcg_ctx->gen_tb);
         tcg_ctx->gen_tb = NULL;
     }
+#endif
+    /*
+     * A hook or plugin callback that left the block by longjmp (a fault
+     * raised from it, qemu_plugin_set_pc(), cpu_loop_exit()) never cleared
+     * its return address into the block.  Left set, a later callback with
+     * no block of its own (a syscall event, a vCPU-loop callback) would
+     * cpu_restore_state() against an unrelated block.
+     */
+    cpu->tcg_hook_ra = 0;
+#ifdef CONFIG_PLUGIN
+    cpu->neg.plugin_cb_ra = 0;
+    cpu->neg.plugin_cb_flags = QEMU_PLUGIN_CB_NO_REGS;
 #endif
     if (bql_locked()) {
         bql_unlock();
